{
  "id": "central-tendency-bias",
  "term": "central-tendency bias",
  "definition": "Central-tendency bias is a pattern in which people judge themselves as being closer to the middle of a distribution than they really are, regardless of their actual position. In the source material, it refers to people placing their income rank near the median even when their objective income rank is higher or lower.",
